 "note": "[agent-bulk] shw 23009 (247.0 MeV, 14 seg, 100.0 cm, reco pdg 211) is over-clustered, and shw23009-az+085-el+20 makes it plain: the yellow member set is TWO spatially disjoint groups with a completely empty gap between them. Group A is the seed alone - 23009, a 26.5 cm pdg-211 stem found by stem_backfill, sitting on the nu vertex inside the orange cluster-23 cloud together with the unowned protons 23002 (23.4 cm) and 23006 (5.5 cm). Group B is thirteen segments 44-96 cm away at 64-102 deg from the shower axis: 24014, 60020, 24013 (22.9 cm), 24015 (17.8 cm), 24011, 76052 (9.2 cm), 67037, 76054, 76055, 68038, 70040 (5.2 cm), 69039, 73043 - i.e. every member except the seed. The axis arrow points one way and the entire body of the shower is off at right angles to it, across charge-free space; this is visible on both azimuths (az-055 and az+085, 140 deg apart), so it is not a projection artifact. All thirteen marked OUT. Group B is a detached EM region ~50-95 cm off the vertex and it plausibly IS a real shower - but it is not this stem's shower, and the reco has stitched a vertex pion stem onto it. Also examined: shw 66036 (103.2 MeV, 6 seg, 19.5 cm, pdg 11 - this is the manifest's em_max, the nominal EM shower of the event), which lives inside group B and reads CORRECT: its acceptance plot has no non-member circle anywhere in range, its members run 0-21.5 cm at 0-16 deg along its own axis with only two small wide-angle absorptions (65025 0.12 cm at 37 deg, 72042 0.56 cm at 35 deg), and the nearest non-members are at 72-151 deg. I put the verdict on 23009 rather than on 66036 because 23009 is the highest-energy in-scope shower and is where the clustering failure is; 66036's finding is stated here instead. Vertex: the star sits where the cluster-23 stem meets the incoming grey track and I see no reason to doubt it. Scope: 2 showers of 10 examined; 8 skipped by the <20 MeV rule and not looked at. The vtx-* sweep is half-span 98 cm here and was used for topology only. Verdict is about clustering; I make no PID claim on either object beyond quoting the reco's own pdg.",
